236
00:22:43,610 --> 00:22:45,510
 No, don't try to fire on it. No, don't.

237
00:22:45,820 --> 00:22:48,070
 In case you didn't notice, there's another one.

238
00:22:48,530 --> 00:22:50,400
 Time limit has expired. What is your answer?

239
00:22:50,970 --> 00:22:52,550
 We accept. I mean refuse.

240
00:22:52,810 --> 00:22:53,630
 No, we surrender.

241
00:22:54,170 --> 00:22:54,530
 Unconditionally?

242
00:22:55,650 --> 00:22:56,010
 Unconditionally.

243
00:22:56,510 --> 00:22:56,940
 Very well.

244
00:22:57,730 --> 00:23:00,990
 Inform the general. We are sending units to Cassiopeia to govern the planet.

245
00:23:01,760 --> 00:23:04,390
 Also send units to take command of your ships.

246
00:23:11,440 --> 00:23:19,360
 Only seven minutes more before the computer blows up and blocks all the exits.

247
00:23:40,520 --> 00:24:12,040
 Fire.

248
00:24:12,990 --> 00:24:15,060
 Spaceship is ready for launching, Captain.

249
00:24:15,340 --> 00:24:17,300
 This is it. Is everybody on board ready?

250
00:24:17,580 --> 00:24:17,900
 Roger.

251
00:24:19,380 --> 00:24:22,150
 Okay, let's go, Metro.

252
00:24:27,800 --> 00:24:34,260
 Now, a little young man, I have a slight difficulty here.

253
00:24:34,520 --> 00:24:36,470
 But I recorded and stored the data.

254
00:24:36,730 --> 00:24:38,170
 4-2-2-3-7-1 on the other.

255
00:24:38,370 --> 00:24:40,330
 And 4-2-3-2-7-1.

256
00:24:40,390 --> 00:24:43,400
 Then again, 4-3-2-2-1-7.

257
00:24:43,400 --> 00:24:44,860
 The permutations are a bore.

258
00:24:45,160 --> 00:24:46,240
 And let's start all over again.

259
00:24:47,070 --> 00:24:50,270
 Metro, we have three minutes before this whole thing blows up.

260
00:24:50,490 --> 00:24:51,010
 Let's go!

261
00:24:51,440 --> 00:24:53,530
 Such a tone of voice. I'm doing my best.

262
00:24:56,350 --> 00:25:01,550
 By 4-2-3-1-7 or 4-3-2-1-7, it isn't all that difficult, surely.

263
00:25:02,030 --> 00:25:03,240
 Metro, two minutes!

264
00:25:03,970 --> 00:25:06,190
 It's like all Cassiopean force is broken.

265
00:25:06,620 --> 00:25:08,820
 Good news for anyone who survives this.

266
00:25:11,600 --> 00:25:12,860
 Nothing, Colonel.

267
00:25:13,310 --> 00:25:14,960
 And all combat has ceased.

268
00:25:15,230 --> 00:25:17,890
 I'm afraid we may have to consider them as lost.

269
00:25:26,270 --> 00:25:33,250
 It's 4-3-2-7-1.

270
00:25:33,450 --> 00:25:34,470
 It had to be that.

271
00:25:34,550 --> 00:25:36,630
 I must have Maestro checked my memory banks.

272
00:25:37,390 --> 00:26:00,280
 It takes so long on such a simple job.

273
00:26:02,510 --> 00:26:07,040
 I'll ask you, who was always forgotten?

274
00:26:14,390 --> 00:26:24,990
 So wonder places.

